    <p>I started goGreenlit because I was tired of watching early-stage companies face a false choice: hire a junior QA engineer they can afford and hope for the best, or skip QA entirely until they hit a production incident that forces the issue. There is a third option, and it is underused.</p>
    <p>This post is my honest take on when each approach makes sense. I have been on both sides – as an in-house QA engineer at startups and as an outsourced QA consultant. I will give you the framework we use when a prospective client asks this question, even when the answer is not goGreenlit.</p>

